tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2463-an-entry-named-main-is-refused-at-its-line.case/main.hero:5:5: error[catalogue_refused]: `use <json>/p` reaches a package through the catalogue, and it does not read: tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2463-an-entry-named-main-is-refused-at-its-line.case/heroes.toml:6: `main` is the entry point every program declares, `function main()`, so a package named so cannot be named from a program: its `use <main>/main` is shadowed by that function, so no line reaches the entry: a folder or a git source takes another name, `[dependencies.<name>]`, which its `use` lines write, and a package of the index keeps the index's name, so one called `main` is reached by no program — a catalogue that does not read names no package, the lines above that one included
